\'(0)\\): \\(\\sqrt{2}\\).  \n  - Curvature: \\(\\kappa = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^3} = \\frac{1}{2}\\).  \n  - The tool can provide this reasoning and the final answer.\n\n**Additional Considerations**  \n- The tool may hallucinate; verify the final answer independently.  \n- The point \\((0,1,0)\\) uniquely corresponds to \\(t=0\\) because \\(\\sinh 0 = 0\\), \\(\\cosh 0 = 1\\), and \\(t=0\\).  \n- The curvature is constant? No, but at this specific point it simplifies nicely.  \n- Ensure the final answer is enclosed in `<answer>` and `</answer>` tags, with no content after.\n\n**Final Answer**  \n<answer>\\(\\kappa = \\frac{1}{2}\\)</answer>\n- **Memory (Tools Used & Results):** {\'Action Step 1\': {\'tool_name\': \'Generalist_Solution_Generator_Tool\', \'sub_goal\': \'Compute the exact curvature of the curve at \\\\(t=0\\\\).\\n\\n4.\', \'command\': \'execution = tool.execute(query="Find the exact curvature of the curve given by the vector function r(t) = (sinh(t), cosh(t), t) at the point (0, 1, 0), which corresponds to t=0. Compute the curvature using the formula κ(t) = |r\\\'(t) × r\\\'\\\'(t)| / |r\\\'(t)|^3, and provide the exact value at t=0.")\', \'result\': ["We are given  \\n\\\\[\\n\\\\mathbf{r}(t) = (\\\\sinh t, \\\\cosh t, t)\\n\\\\]  \\nand we want the curvature at \\\\(t = 0\\\\).\\n\\n**Step 1: First derivative**  \\n\\\\[\\n\\\\mathbf{r}\'(t) = (\\\\cosh t, \\\\sinh t, 1)\\n\\\\]  \\nAt \\\\(t=0\\\\):  \\n\\\\[\\n\\\\mathbf{r}\'(0) = (\\\\cosh 0, \\\\sinh 0, 1) = (1, 0, 1)\\n\\\\]\\n\\n**Step 2: Second derivative**  \\n\\\\[\\n\\\\mathbf{r}\'\'(t) = (\\\\sinh t, \\\\cosh t, 0)\\n\\\\]  \\nAt \\\\(t=0\\\\):  \\n\\\\[\\n\\\\mathbf{r}\'\'(0) = (0, 1, 0)\\n\\\\]\\n\\n**Step 3: Cross product \\\\(\\\\mathbf{r}\'(0) \\\\times \\\\mathbf{r}\'\'(0)\\\\)**  \\n\\\\[\\n(1,0,1) \\\\times (0,1,0) =\\n\\\\begin{vmatrix}\\n\\\\mathbf{i} & \\\\mathbf{j} & \\\\mathbf{k} \\\\\\\\\\n1 & 0 & 1 \\\\\\\\\\n0 & 1 & 0\\n\\\\end{vmatrix}\\n\\\\]  \\n\\\\[\\n= \\\\m