ue of a complex function at a specific point, which requires algebraic manipulation and limit evaluation. Given that the Generalist_Solution_Generator_Tool is equipped to handle such tasks step-by-step, it is the best tool for this task. The sub-goal should focus on computing the residue using known techniques from complex analysis.\n\n2. **Context:**  \n- The function \\( f(z) = \\frac{z}{z^6 + 1} \\).\n- We need to find the residue at \\( z = i \\).\n\n3. **Sub-Goal:**  \nCompute and output the residue of \\( f(z) = \\frac{z}{z^6 + 1} \\) at \\( z = i \\).\n\n4. **Tool Name:**  \nGeneralist_Solution_Generator_Tool", 'prompt_token_ids': [151644, 8948, 198, 2610, 525, 264, 10950, 11, 11521, 11, 323, 7785, 17847, 13, 151645, 198, 151644, 872, 271, 6262, 25, 29901, 279, 22823, 1790, 3019, 311, 2621, 279, 3239, 1667, 2500, 7375, 323, 3681, 7354, 382, 1972, 510, 12, 3070, 2859, 66963, 7379, 279, 48132, 315, 279, 729, 17767, 1124, 37018, 90, 89, 15170, 89, 61, 21, 10, 16, 92, 1124, 8, 518, 279, 1459, 17767, 1147, 21397, 1124, 568, 3197, 5527, 11, 2550, 279, 1590, 4226, 43810, 304, 366, 9217, 29, 323, 690, 9217, 29, 9492, 13, 3155, 537, 6923, 894, 2213, 1283, 279, 690, 9217, 29, 4772, 624, 12, 3070, 2859, 18320, 66963, 3070, 19237, 315, 279, 11361, 66963, 2303, 785, 1196, 17064, 311, 1477, 279, 48132, 315, 279, 729, 17767, 282, 13174, 8, 284, 1124, 37018, 90, 89, 15170, 89, 61, 21, 10, 16, 92, 1124, 8, 518, 279, 1459, 17767, 1147, 284, 600, 1124, 568, 1096, 374, 264, 6351, 6358, 3491, 22703, 34447, 315, 264, 48132, 518, 264, 4285, 25026, 382, 334, 45, 20122, 30240, 66963, 2303, 16, 13, 3070, 31137, 18320, 1365, 1800, 60607, 30435, 334, 1365, 2014, 10542, 279, 25026, 1973, 323, 12564, 279, 48132, 1667, 279, 14806, 369, 4285, 50779, 25, 1124, 11520, 1318, 90, 1061, 25547, 69, 11, 600, 8, 284, 1124, 4659, 15159, 89, 1124, 983, 600, 92, 320, 89, 17600, 8, 282, 13174, 10699, 568, 2303, 17, 13, 3070, 2101, 26083, 292, 60911, 2914, 334, 1365, 2014, 8168, 17767, 89, 61, 21, 10, 1