 Residue at a simple pole\\nFor a simple pole at \\\\( z_0 \\\\),  \\n\\\\[\\n\\\\text{Res}(f, z_0) = \\\\lim_{z \\\\to z_0} (z - z_0) f(z).\\n\\\\]  \\nHere \\\\( f(z) = \\\\frac{z}{z^6+1} \\\\), so  \\n\\\\[\\n\\\\text{Res}(f, i) = \\\\lim_{z \\\\to i} (z - i) \\\\frac{z}{z^6+1}.\\n\\\\]  \\nSince \\\\( z^6+1 = (z-i)(\\\\text{nonzero factor}) \\\\), we can use  \\n\\\\[\\n\\\\text{Res}(f, i) = \\\\frac{i}{(z^6+1)\'\\\\big|_{z=i}} = \\\\frac{i}{6i^5}.\\n\\\\]\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Step 4: Compute\\nWe have \\\\( i^5 = i \\\\), so  \\n\\\\[\\n6i^5 = 6i.\\n\\\\]  \\nThus  \\n\\\\[\\n\\\\text{Res}(f, i) = \\\\frac{i}{6i} = \\\\frac{1}{6}.\\n\\\\]\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{\\\\frac{1}{6}}\\n\\\\]"]}}\n\nInstructions:\n1. Review the query and the results from all actions.\n2. Synthesize the key findings into a clear, step-by-step summary of the process.\n3. Provide a direct, precise answer to the original query.\n\nOutput Structure:\n1.  **Process Summary:** A clear, step-by-step breakdown of how the query was addressed, including the purpose and key results of each action.\n2.  **Answer:** A direct and concise final answer to the query.\n', 'gen_ai.response.id': 'afabcc7a-1d82-44dc-ab66-54fb15179c4d', 'gen_ai.response.model': 'deepseek-v4-flash', 'gen_ai.openai.system_fingerprint': 'a26a7955944dc5c60445bff77fac9c8e', 'gen_ai.usage.total_tokens': 2079, 'gen_ai.usage.prompt_tokens': 1789, 'gen_ai.usage.completion_tokens': 290, 'gen_ai.completion.0.finish_reason': 'stop', 'gen_ai.completion.0.role': 'assistant', 'gen_ai.completion.0.content': "**Process Summary:**  \nTo find the residue of \\( f(z) = \\frac{z}{z^6+1} \\) at \\( z = i \\), the solution involved:  \n1. **Factoring \\( z^6 + 1 \\):** Solving \\( z^6 = -1 \\) gives six roots, one of which is \\( z = i \\) (corresponding to \\( k=1 \\)).  \n2. **Confirming the pole is simple:** The derivative \\( 6z^5 \\) at \\( z = i \\) is \\( 6i \\neq 0 \\), so \\( z = i \\) is a simple pole.  \n3. **Applying the residue formula for simple poles:**  \n   \\[\n   \\text{Res}(f, i) = \\lim_{z \\to i} (z - i) \\frac{z}{z^6+1} = \\frac{i}{(z^6+1)'|_{z=i}} = \\frac{i}{6i^5}.\n   \\]  \n4. **Simplifying:** Since \\( i^5 = i \\), we get \\( \\frac{i}{6i} = \\frac{1}{6} \\).\n\n**Answer:**  \n<answer>  \nThe residue of \\( \\frac{z}{z^6+1} \\) at \\( z = i \\) is \\( \\frac{1}{6} \\).  \n</answer>"}, 'events': [], 'links': [], 'resource': {'attributes': {'service.name': 'agentops', 'agentops.project.id': 'dummy', 'imported_libraries': ['string', 'sympy', 'uuid', 'json', 'asyncio']}, 'schema_url': ''}}, {'name': 'agentops_reward_operation.task', 'context': {'trace_id': '0xcd25701358303365c33bcc4395b49d45', 'span_id': '0x34ede6f762f3fa3d', 'trace_state': '[]'}, 'kind': 'SpanKind.INTERNAL', 'parent_id': '0x5aab183f0c2dd78f', 'start_time': '2026-08-25T15:27:40.167652Z', 'end_time': '2026-08-25T15:27:40.167869Z', 'status': {'status_code': 'UNSET'}, 'attributes': {'agentops.span.kind': 'task', 'operation.name': 'agentops_reward_operation', 'agentops.task.input': '{"args": [], "kwargs": {}}', 'agentops.task.output': '{"type": "reward", "value": 1.0}'}, 'events': [], 'links': [], 'resource': {'attributes': {'service.name': 'agentops', 'agentops.project.id': 'dummy', 'imported_libraries': ['string', 'sympy', 'uuid', 'json', 'asyncio']}, 'schema_url': ''}}] logs=None metadata={}[36m(TaskRunner pid=237025)[0m INFO:2026-08-25 23:27:44,886:127.0.0.1 - - [25/Aug/2026 23:27:44] "POST /v1/chat/completions HTTP/1.1" 200 -

