):\\n\\n\\\\(s^2 = 97.515625\\\\), \\\\(s^3 = 962.939453125\\\\)  \\n\\\\(92(962.939453125) = 88590.4296875\\\\)  \\n\\\\(729(97.515625) = 71088.890625\\\\)  \\n\\\\(11178(9.875) = 110376.75\\\\)  \\nSum: \\\\(88590.4296875 - 71088.890625 = 17501.5390625\\\\)  \\n\\\\(17501.5390625 - 110376.75 = -92875.2109375\\\\)  \\n\\\\(-92875.2109375 + 93015 = 139.7890625\\\\)  \\nPositive.\\n\\nTry \\\\(s = \\\\frac{157}{16} = 9.8125\\\\):\\n\\n\\\\(s^2 = 96.28515625\\\\), \\\\(s^3 = 944.7978515625\\\\)  \\n\\\\(92(944.7978515625) = 86921.40234375\\\\)  \\n\\\\(729(96.28515625) = 70191.87890625\\\\)  \\n\\\\(11178(9.8125) = 109684.125\\\\)  \\nSum: \\\\(86921.40234375 - 70191.87890625 = 16729.5234375\\\\)  \\n\\\\(16729.5234375 - 109684.125 = -92954.6015625\\\\)  \\n\\\\(-92954.6015625 + 93015 = 60.3984375\\\\)  \\nPositive.\\n\\nTry \\\\(s = \\\\frac{39}{4} = 9.75\\\\) gave 10, so root is slightly above 9.75.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Step 10: Use symmetry to guess exact fraction**\\n\\nThe cubic might factor nicely. Let’s try \\\\(s = \\\\frac{39}{4}\\\\) gave 10, so maybe \\\\(s = \\\\frac{39}{4} + \\\\epsilon\\\\) with small \\\\(\\\\epsilon\\\\).  \\nInstead, solve exactly:  \\nWe have  \\n\\\\[\\n92 s^3 - 729 s^2 - 11178 s + 93015 = 0\\n\\\\]\\n\\nCheck if \\\\(s = \\\\frac{23}{2} = 11.5\\\\)? No, too big.\\n\\nTry \\\\(s = \\\\frac{27}{3} = 9\\\\) gave 432, not zero.\\n\\nMaybe factor by grouping:  \\nTry \\\\(s = \\\\frac{15}{2} = 7.5\\\\):  \\n\\\\(92(421.875) = 38812.5\\\\)  \\n\\\\(729(56.25) = 41006.25\\\\)  \\n\\\\(11178(7.5) = 83835\\\\)  \\nSum: \\\\(38812.5 - 41006.25 = -2193.75\\\\)  \\n\\\\(-2193.75 - 83835 = -86028.75\\\\)  \\n\\\\(-86028.75 + 93015 = 6986.25\\\\)  \\nNot zero.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Step 11: Use calculus to find max \\\\(s\\\\)**\\n\\nWe want max \\\\(s\\\\) such that cubic has 3 positive roots. The boundary is when two roots coincide (discriminant zero).  \\nThat means two of \\\\(a,b,c\\\\) are equal. Let \\\\(a=b=x\\\\), \\\\(c=y\\\\).\\n\\nThen:\\n\\\\[