down into subtasks and use the tool multiple times.\\n5. Use it as a starting point for complex tasks, then refine with specialized tools.\\n6. Verify important information from its responses.\\n"}, \'require_llm_engine\': True}\n- **Relevant Data:** - No additional context is needed as this step involves using a general solution generator tool.\n\n3.\n\nInstructions:\n1.  Analyze the tool\'s required parameters from its metadata.\n2.  Construct valid Python code that addresses the sub-goal using the provided context and data.\n3.  The command must include at least one call to `tool.execute()`.\n4.  Each `tool.execute()` call must be assigned to a variable named **`execution`**.\n5.  Please give the exact numbers and parameters should be used in the `tool.execute()` call.\n\nOutput Format:\nPresent your response in the following structured format. Do not include any extra text or explanations.\n\nGenerated Command:\n```python\n<command>\n```\n\nExample1:\nGenerated Command:\n```python\nexecution = tool.execute(query="Summarize the following porblom:"Isaac has 100 toys, masa gets ...., how much are their together?")\n```\n\nExample2:\nGenerated Command:\n```python\nexecution = tool.execute(query=["Methanol", "function of hyperbola", "Fermat\'s Last Theorem"])\n```\n', 'gen_ai.response.id': '077067d0-a9a4-4f56-acb4-2ae8cfe24bf2', 'gen_ai.response.model': 'deepseek-v4-flash', 'gen_ai.openai.system_fingerprint': 'a26a7955944dc5c60445bff77fac9c8e', 'gen_ai.usage.total_tokens': 885, 'gen_ai.usage.prompt_tokens': 802, 'gen_ai.usage.completion_tokens': 83, 'gen_ai.completion.0.finish_reason': 'stop', 'gen_ai.completion.0.role': 'assistant', 'gen_ai.completion.0.content': 'Generated Command:\n```python\nexecution = tool.execute(query="Find the number of triples of nonnegative integers (a,b,c) satisfying a + b + c = 300 and a^2b + a^2c + b^2a + b^2c + c^2a + c^2b = 6,000,000. Provide a step-by-step solution.")\n```'}, 'events': [], 'links': [], 'resource': {'attributes': {'service.name': 'agentops', 'agentops.project.id': 'dummy', 'imported_libraries': ['string', 'sympy', 'uuid', 'json', 'asyncio']}, 'schema_url': ''}}, {'name': 'openai.chat.completion', 'context': {'trace_id': '0xcacfd3d8feef3e7814e3ef65c326153d', 'span_id': '0xaaa1f38b52ff78eb', 'trace_state': '[]'}, 'kind': 'SpanKind.CLIENT', 'parent_id': None, 'start_time': '2026-08-25T15:31:28.473725Z', 'end_time': '2026-08-25T15:31:39.937988Z', 'status': {'status_code': 'OK'}, 'attributes': {'gen_ai.request.type': 'chat', 'gen_ai.system': 'OpenAI', 'gen_ai.request.model': 'deepseek-v4-flash', 'gen_ai.request.max_tokens': 4000, 'gen_ai.request.temperature': 0, 'gen_ai.request.top_p': 0.99, 'gen_ai.request.streaming': False, 'gen_ai.prompt.0.role': 'system', 'gen_ai.prompt.0.content': 'You are a helpful assistant.', 'gen_ai.prompt.1.role': 'user', 'gen_ai.prompt.1.content': 'Find the number of triples of nonnegative integers (a,b,c) satisfying a + b + c = 300 and a^2b + a^2c + b^2a + b^2c + c^2a + c^2b = 6,000,000. Provide a step-by-step solution.', 'gen_ai.response.id': 'f24bdc4e-c8db-40ed-a99b-47d991423fe0', 'gen_ai.response.model': 'deepseek-v4-flash', 'gen_ai.openai.system_fingerprint': 'a26a7955944dc5c60445bff77fac9c8e', 'gen_ai.usage.total_tokens': 1538, 'gen_ai.usage.prompt_tokens': 79, 'gen_ai.usage.completion_tokens': 1459, 'gen_ai.completion.0.finish_reason': 'stop', 'gen_ai.completion.0.role': 'assistant', 'gen_ai.completion.0.content': 'We are given:\n\n\\[\na + b + c = 300\n\\]\nand\n\\[\na^2b + a^2c + b^2a + b^2c + c^2a + c^2b = 6{,}000{,}000.\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Symmetry and rewriting\nThe second equation can be factored. Notice:\n\n\\[\na^2b + a^2c + b^2a + b^2c + c^2a + c^2b\n= ab(a+b) + ac(a+c) + bc(b+c).\n\\]\n\nBut also, since \\(a+b+c = 300\\), we have:\n\n\\[\na+b = 300 - c, \\quad a+c = 300 - b, \\quad b+c = 300 - a.\n\\]\n\nSo:\n\n\\[\nab(a+b) + ac(a+c) + bc(b+c) \n= ab(300 - c) + ac(300 - b) + bc(300 - a).\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Expand\nExpand:\n\n\\[\n= 300ab - abc + 300ac - abc + 300bc - abc\n\\]\n\\[\n= 300(ab + ac + bc) - 3abc.\n\\]\n\nSo the equation becomes:\n\n\\[\n300(ab + ac + bc) - 3abc = 6{,}000{,}000.\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Divide by 3\n\\[\n100(ab + ac + bc) - abc = 2{,}000{,}000.\n\\]\n\nThus:\n\n\\[\nabc = 100(ab + ac + bc) - 2{,}000{,}000.\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Use symmetric sums\nLet:\n\\[\ns = a+b+c = 300,\n\\]\n\\[\np = ab + bc + ca,\n\\]\n\\[\nr = abc.\n\\]\n\nWe have:\n\\[\nr = 100p - 2{,}000{,}000.\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### Step 5: Cubic with roots \\(a,b,c\\)\nThe cubic with roots \\(a,b,c\\) is:\n\n\\[\nx^3 - s x^2 + p x - r = 0\n\\]\n\\[\nx^3 - 300x^2 + p x - (100p - 2{,}000{,}000) = 0.\n\\]\n\nSo:\n\n\\[\nx^3 - 300x^2 + p x - 100p + 2{,}000{,}000 = 0.\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### Step 6: Factor by grouping\nGroup terms:\n\n\\[\n(x^3 - 300x^2) + (p x - 100p) + 2{,}000{,}000 = 0\n\\]\n\\[\nx^2(x - 300) + p(x - 100) + 2{,}000{,}000 = 0.\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### Step 7: Try integer roots\nSince \\(a,b,c\\) are nonnegative integers, try small divisors of \\(2{,}000{,}000\\) that might satisfy.\n\nCheck \\(x = 100\\):\n\\[\n100^2(100 - 300) + p(100 - 100) + 2{,}000{,}000\n= 10{,}000(-200) + 0 + 2{,}000{,}000 = -2{,}000{,}000 + 2{,}000{,}000 = 0.\n\\]\nSo \\(x=100\\) is a root.\n\n---\n\n### Step 8: Factor out \\(x-100\\)\nDivide \\(x^3 - 300x^2 + p x - 100p + 2{,}000{,}000\\) by \\(x-100\\):\n\nUsing synthetic division with 100:\n\nCoefficients: \\(1, -300, p, -100p + 2{,}000{,}000\\).\n\nBring down 1.  \nMultiply by 100: \\(100\\), add to -300 → \\(-200\\).  \nMultiply by 100: \\(-20{,}000\\), add to \\(p\\) → \\(p - 20{,}000\\).  \nMultiply by 100: \\(100p - 2{,}000{,}000\\), add to \\(-100p + 2{,}000{,}000\\) → 0.\n\nSo quotient is:\n\n\\[\nx^2 - 200x + (p - 20{,}000).\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### Step 9: Roots of quadratic\nThe other two roots \\(a,b\\) satisfy:\n\n\\[\na + b = 200, \\quad ab = p - 20{,}000.\n\\]\n\nBut we also have \\(a+b+c = 300\\) and \\(c=100\\), so indeed \\(a+b=200\\).\n\n---\n\n### Step 10: Find \\(p\\)\nWe know \\(p = ab + bc + ca = ab + 100(a+b) = ab + 100 \\cdot 200 = ab + 20{,}000\\).\n\nFrom quadratic: \\(ab = p - 20{,}000\\), so this is consistent.\n\n---\n\n### Step 11: Nonnegative integer solutions for \\(a,b\\)\nWe need \\(a+b=200\\), \\(a,b \\ge 0\\) integers.  \nNumber of nonnegative integer solutions: \\(a\\) can be \\(0,1,\\dots,200\\), so \\(201\\) solutions.\n\n---\n\n### Step 12: Check if any restriction from \\(abc\\) formula\nWe have \\(abc = 100 \\cdot ab\\) (since \\(c=100\\)).  \nFrom earlier: \\(abc = 100p - 2{,}000{,}000\\).  \nBut \\(p = ab + 20{,}000\\), so:\n\n\\[\n100(ab + 20{,}000) - 2{,}000{,}000 = 100ab + 2{,}000{,}000 - 2{,}000{,}000 = 100ab.\n\\]\nMatches \\(abc = 100ab\\). So no extra restriction.\n\n---\n\n### Step 13: Count triples\nEach \\((a,b)\\) with \\(a+b=200\\) gives a triple \\((a,b,100)\\).  \nSince the original equation is symmetric in \\(a,b,c\\), but here \\(c\\) is fixed as 100, each unordered triple with two equal numbers might be counted multiple times.\n\nWe must count ordered triples \\((a,b,c)\\):\n\n- If \\(a \\neq b\\), then \\((a,b,100)\\) and \\((b,a,100)\\) are distinct ordered triples.\n- If \\(a = b = 100\\), then \\((100,100,100)\\) is just one triple.\n\nNumber of ordered pairs \\((a,b)\\) with \\(a+b=200\\) is 201.  \nAmong them, \\(a=b=100\\) is one case.  \nSo distinct ordered triples: \\(201\\) total.\n\n---\n\n### Step 14: Final answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{201}\n\\]'}, 'events': [], 'links': [], 'resource': {'attributes': {'service.name': 'agentops', 'agentops.project.id': 'dummy', 'imported_libraries': ['string', 'sympy', 'uuid', 'json', 'asyncio']}, 'schema_url': ''}}, {'name': 'openai.chat.completion', 'context': {'trace_id': '0xcd25701358303365c33bcc4395b49d45', 'span_id': '0x1da130c3223a0496', 'trace_state': '[]'}, 'kind': 'SpanKind.CLIENT', 'parent_id': '0x5aab183f0c2dd78f', 'start_time': '2026-08-25T15:31:39.939775Z', 'end_time': '2026-08-25T15:31:42.245399Z', 'status': {'status_