\\):  \\n  For \\\\(|x| \\\\le \\\\frac12\\\\), \\\\(f(x) = \\\\frac12 - |x|\\\\).  \\n  For \\\\(|x| \\\\ge \\\\frac12\\\\), \\\\(f(x) = |x| - \\\\frac12\\\\).  \\n  So \\\\(f\\\\) is even, has a “V” shape with minimum 0 at \\\\(|x| = \\\\frac12\\\\), maximum \\\\(\\\\frac12\\\\) at \\\\(x=0\\\\), and grows linearly beyond.\\n\\n- \\\\(g(x)\\\\):  \\n  For \\\\(|x| \\\\le \\\\frac14\\\\), \\\\(g(x) = \\\\frac14 - |x|\\\\).  \\n  For \\\\(|x| \\\\ge \\\\frac14\\\\), \\\\(g(x) = |x| - \\\\frac14\\\\).  \\n  So \\\\(g\\\\) is even, minimum 0 at \\\\(|x| = \\\\frac14\\\\), maximum \\\\(\\\\frac14\\\\) at \\\\(x=0\\\\).\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Step 2 – Composition \\\\(g(f(t))\\\\)\\n\\nLet \\\\(u = f(t)\\\\). Since \\\\(f(t) \\\\ge 0\\\\), we have \\\\(|u| = u\\\\).\\n\\nSo:\\n\\\\[\\ng(f(t)) = g(u) = \\n\\\\begin{cases}\\n\\\\frac14 - u, & 0 \\\\le u \\\\le \\\\frac14 \\\\\\\\\\nu - \\\\frac14, & u \\\\ge \\\\frac14\\n\\\\end{cases}\\n\\\\]\\n\\nNow \\\\(u = f(t)\\\\) ranges from 0 to \\\\(\\\\frac12\\\\) (since \\\\(f\\\\) max is \\\\(\\\\frac12\\\\)).\\n\\nSo:\\n\\n- If \\\\(0 \\\\le f(t) \\\\le \\\\frac14\\\\): \\\\(g(f(t)) = \\\\frac14 - f(t)\\\\).\\n- If \\\\(\\\\frac14 \\\\le f(t) \\\\le \\\\frac12\\\\): \\\\(g(f(t)) = f(t) - \\\\frac14\\\\).\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Step 3 – When is \\\\(f(t) \\\\le \\\\frac14\\\\)?\\n\\n\\\\(f(t) = \\\\big||t| - \\\\frac12\\\\big| \\\\le \\\\frac14\\\\) means:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n-\\\\frac14 \\\\le |t| - \\\\frac12 \\\\le \\\\frac14\\n\\\\]\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\frac14 \\\\le |t| \\\\le \\\\frac34\\n\\\\]\\n\\nSo for \\\\(|t| \\\\in [\\\\frac14, \\\\frac34]\\\\), \\\\(g(f(t)) = \\\\frac14 - f(t)\\\\).\\n\\nFor \\\\(|t| < \\\\frac14\\\\) or \\\\(|t| > \\\\frac34\\\\), \\\\(f(t) > \\\\frac14\\\\) and \\\\(g(f(t)) = f(t) - \\\\frac14\\\\).\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Step 4 – First equation: \\\\(y = 4 g(f(\\\\sin(2\\\\pi x)))\\\\)\\n\\nLet \\\\(t = \\\\sin(2\\\\pi x)\\\\). This is periodic with period 1 in \\\\(x\\\\), range \\\\([-1,1]\\\\), symmetric.\\n\\nWe need