problem is a classic complex analysis/optimization exercise; the maximum real part is likely a nice integer or rational number.  \n- Ensure the tool uses \\(|z|=4\\) correctly and does not confuse with \\(|z|=1\\) or other radii.  \n- The expression involves two terms; the maximum may occur at a specific \\(\\theta\\) that can be found by setting the derivative to zero.\n</answer>\n- **Available Tools:** [\'Generalist_Solution_Generator_Tool\']\n- **Toolbox Metadata:** {\'Generalist_Solution_Generator_Tool\': {\'tool_name\': \'Generalist_Solution_Generator_Tool\', \'tool_description\': \'A generalized tool that takes query from the user, and answers the question step by step to the best of its ability. It can also accept an image.\', \'tool_version\': \'1.0.0\', \'input_types\': {\'query\': \'str - The query that includes query from the user to guide the agent to generate response.\'}, \'output_type\': \'str - The generated response to the original query\', \'demo_commands\': [{\'command\': \'execution = tool.execute(query="Summarize the following text in a few lines")\', \'description\': \'Generate a short summary given the query from the user.\'}], \'user_metadata\': {\'limitation\': \'\\nThe Generalist_Solution_Generator_Tool may provide hallucinated or incorrect responses.\\n\', \'best_practice\': "\\nFor optimal results with the Generalist_Solution_Generator_Tool:\\n1. Use it for general queries or tasks that don\'t require s\n...[context truncated]...\ned knowledge or specific tools in the toolbox.\\n2. Provide clear, specific query.   \\n3. Use it to answer the original query through step by step reasoning for tasks without complex or multi-step reasoning.\\n4. For complex queries, break them down into subtasks and use the tool multiple times.\\n5. Use it as a starting point for complex tasks, then refine with specialized tools.\\n6. Verify important information from its responses.\\n"}, \'require_llm_engine\': True}}\n- **Previous Steps:** {}\n\nInstructions:\n1. Analyze the query, previous steps, and available tools.\n2. Select the **single best tool** for the next step.\n3. Formulate a specific, achievable **sub-goal** for that tool.\n4. Provide all necessary **context** (data, file names, variables) for the tool to function.\n\nResponse Format:\n1.  **Justification:** Explain your choice of tool and sub-goal.\n2.  **Context:** Provide all necessary information for the tool.\n3.  **Sub-Goal:** State the specific objective for the tool.\n4.  **Tool Name:** State the exact name of the selected tool.\n\nRules:\n- Select only ONE tool.\n- The sub-goal must be directly achievable by the selected tool.\n- The Context section must contain all information the tool needs to function.\n- The response must end with the Context, Sub-Goal, and Tool Name sections in that order, with no extra content.\n                    ', 'gen_ai.response.id': 'chatcmpl-bdfd775ac8884f08a0fffca99c66ea4a', 'gen_ai.response.model': 'models/Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct', 'gen_ai.usage.total_tokens': 1384, 'gen_ai.usage.prompt_tokens': 1031, 'gen_ai.usage.completion_tokens': 353, 'gen_ai.completion.0.finish_reason': 'stop', 'gen_ai.completion.0.role': 'assistant', 'gen_ai.completion.0.content': '1. **Justification:** The query involves finding the maximum real part of a complex expression where \\(z\\) is constrained to have a modulus of 4. This problem can be effectively solved by parameterizing \\(z\\) using its polar form and then maximizing the real part of the given expression over all possible values of \\(\\theta\\). The Generalist_Solution_Generator_Tool can handle this step-by-step approach, even though it may not directly provide the exact maximum value due to its limitations.\n\n2. **Context:** We need to find the maximum possible real part of the expression \\((75+117i)z + \\frac{96+144i}{z}\\) where \\(|z|=4\\). We will use \\(z = 4e^{i\\theta}\\) for parameterization.\n\n3. **Sub-Goal:** Compute and maximize the real part of \\((75+117i)(4e^{i\\theta}) + (96+144i)\\left(\\frac{1}{4e^{i\\theta}}\\right)\\).\n\n4. **Tool Name:** Generalist_Solution_Generator_Tool\n\n(Context, Sub-Goal, Tool Name)\n<answer>\nTo find the optimal next step, we need to parameterize \\( z = 4e^{i\\theta} \\) where \\( |z| = 2008/|96 + 108 i| = 2008/\\sqrt{3^2 + (-2)^2} = 38/3 \\), which simplifies our computation as we are only interested in maximizing over a circle with radius determined by normalization constraints.\n</answer>', 'prompt_token_ids': [151644, 8948, 198, 2610, 525, 264, 10950, 11, 11521, 11, 323, 7785, 17847, 13, 151645, 198, 151644, 872, 271, 6262, 25, 29901, 279, 22823, 1790, 3019, 311, 2621, 279, 3239, 1667, 2500, 7375, 323, 3681, 7354, 382, 1972, 510, 12, 3070, 2859, 66963, 7379, 279, 7772, 3204, 1931, 949, 315, 1124, 9697, 22, 20, 10, 16, 16, 22, 72, 8, 89, 488, 1124, 37018, 90, 24, 21, 10, 16, 19, 19, 72, 15170, 89, 11035, 60, 1380, 400, 89, 3, 374, 264, 6351, 1372, 448, 400, 91, 89, 87803, 19, 3, 382, 4498, 5527, 11, 2550, 279, 1590, 4226, 43810, 304, 366, 9217, 29, 323, 690, 9217, 29, 9492, 13, 3155, 537, 6923, 894, 2213, 1283, 279, 690, 9217, 29, 4772, 13, 3197, 5527, 11, 2550, 279, 1590, 4226, 43810, 304, 366, 9217, 29, 323, 690, 9217, 29, 9492, 13, 3155, 537, 6923, 894, 2213, 1283, 279, 690, 9217, 29, 4772, 624, 12, 3070, 2859, 18320, 66963, 366, 9217, 397, 334, 19237, 315, 11361, 66963, 2303, 785, 3239, 17064, 369, 279, 7772, 3204, 1931, 949, 315, 279, 7493, 1124, 1188, 22, 20, 10, 16, 16, 22, 72, 8, 89, 488, 1124, 37018, 90, 24, 21, 10, 16, 19, 19, 72, 15170, 89, 11035, 701, 1380, 17767, 89, 57758, 374, 264, 6351, 1372, 448, 17767, 91, 89, 87803, 19, 59, 568, 1096, 374, 264, 35972, 25262, 3491, 916, 6351, 5109, 382, 334, 45, 20122, 30240, 66963, 2303, 16, 13, 3070, 31137, 1372, 46876, 334, 1365, 311, 36635, 279, 7493, 11, 8651, 1931, 14, 28016, 3287, 5479, 11, 323, 3705, 12804, 553, 17767, 89, 59, 568, 2303, 17, 13, 3070, 21367, 65964, 320, 5416, 41349, 476, 46876, 292, 32295, 1365, 311, 1477, 279, 71